# Strike acid blobs with a MAGICAL long sword and read the sword's own
# description page before and after (bd inc-m2zi).
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/dequ-hardness-magic.keys 5
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED, and why this is the other half of
# tools/keys/dequ-hardness-plain.keys. Against a monster whose A_DEQU carries
# no save DC, a NON-magical item now has its hardness bypassed; a MAGICAL one
# keeps it. The plain run alone cannot tell that rule from "every item's
# hardness is bypassed", which is why this run exists.
#
# WHY THE HOLY AVENGER. Wizard mode cannot type a plus onto a weapon: "Add
# Quality to Weapon" refuses WQ_KEEN below character level 5, and WQ_IMPACT was
# measured still printing a bypassed hardness. The Holy Avenger is built on the
# SAME base item as the plain half -- its page reads "Long Sword, Holy Avenger
# +2" -- and it carries an effect id, which is the plainest thing
# Item::isMagic tests. tools/keys/luckblade-plus.keys already acquires and
# wields a specific weapon this way and this copies that sequence.
#
# READ THE NUMBERS, NOT THE ADJECTIVE. The Holy Avenger arrives with 38 of 35
# hit points -- item generation sets its plus after its hit points -- so the
# game already calls it "Mildly Damaged" before a blow is struck. The check
# compares the hit-point figures, which that quirk leaves alone, and requires
# that the word "Melted" never appears.
#
# THE GUARD THAT MATTERS. "The magical sword was not damaged" proves nothing if
# the retaliation never reached it. The strike screens are dumped as well, and
# the check requires "Acid splashes the" -- the line the game prints when the
# ITEM is the victim. When the retaliation lands on the striker instead it
# reads "Acid splashes you!", so the two cases cannot be confused.
#
# ONE BLOB PER BLOW, for the reasons dequ-hardness-plain.keys sets out.

@include dequ-setup.keys

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*10                # walk the glyph row to specific (magical) weapons
@until "Holy Avenger" DOWN
DOWN                    # the wanted row is the middle of three; step onto it
ENTER
0                       # Enter Item Level: 0 leaves the sword's own plus alone
ENTER
b                       # Weapon Hand -- the slot lettering skips 'd' (Drop)
SPACE                   # swap the sword into it
@while "two-handed" n
s                       # stow the starting knife the swap pushed into the air
@until "SPACE:Swap" i    # the inventory manager, if it is not already open
@until ">>b)Weapon" b    # select the Weapon Hand
@until "base value of" x # Examine: the item's own description page
@dump:magic-before
@until "Things in View" ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Jellies"
@choose "acid blob"
RIGHT ENTER
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@dump:magic-strike-1

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Jellies"
@choose "acid blob"
RIGHT ENTER
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@dump:magic-strike-2

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Jellies"
@choose "acid blob"
RIGHT ENTER
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@dump:magic-strike-3

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Jellies"
@choose "acid blob"
RIGHT ENTER
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@dump:magic-strike-4

@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>b)Weapon" b
@until "base value of" x
@dump:magic-after
@until "Things in View" ESC
@quit
